<p>NOTES: Full company name is Quaker City Bancorp Inc.</p>
<p>Periods ended June 30.</p>
<p>1997 fiscal year earnings were down primarily because of a special assessment of $3.1 million for recapitalization of the Savings Association Insurance Fund. Excluding the assessment, year earnings would have been $4.6 million, or $1 per share.</p>
<p>Assets at June 30 were $801.4 million versus $725.1 million.</p>
<p>Q4 return on equity improved to 8.49 pct from 6.0 pct, and for year 6.76 pct vs 5.25 pct.</p>
<p>Q4 return on assets improved to 0.75 pct from 0.58 pct, and for year 0.61 pct vs 0.53 pct.</p>
<p>Nonperforming assets were reduced to $10.5 million at quarter end versus $13.1 million a year earlier.</p>
